> This is happening because of
> 
> https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/ebee0a4b66d1b4dba9c51165e78d22fbf3b90d3e/extensions/cache/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/cache/runtime/CacheInterceptor.java#L165
> .
> 
> @mkouba what is the proper pattern to use here?

It surely does not make sense for a `@Singleton` implementation that is designed to be shared... although it's legal. And since the [docs](https://quarkus.io/guides/cache#generating-a-cache-key-with-cachekeygenerator) mention that _"All CDI scopes supported by Quarkus can be used on a key generator."_ the logic should be fixed.

It would make sense to destroy `@Dependent` beans only (which cannot be shared anyway).

The easies way to do this would be something like:
```java
Instance<T> keyGenInstance = keyGenerator.select(keyGeneratorClass);
if (keyGenInstance.isResolvable()) {
   LOGGER.tracef("Using cache key generator bean from Arc [class=%s]", keyGeneratorClass.getName());
   Handle<T> keyGen = keyGenInstance.getHandle();
   try {
      return keyGen.get().generate(method, methodParameterValues);
   } finally {
      // Quarkus-specific
      keyGen.close();
      // Spec-compliant
      InjectableBean<T> bean = keyGen.getBean();
      if (bean == null || Dependent.class.equals(bean.getScope())) {
         destroy();
       }
   }
}
```

OT: It's not exactly clear to name a `@Singleton` implementation `RequestContextKeyGenerator` :D
